{"name":"Electric Pickle","hex":"#00ff04","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, produced by, operated with, or utilising electricity; electrical.","Of or relating to an electronic version of a musical instrument that has an acoustic equivalent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electricity; the electricity supply.","An electric powered version of something that was originally or is more commonly not electric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric"},{"term":"pickle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cucumber preserved in a solution, usually a brine or a vinegar syrup.","Any vegetable preserved in vinegar and consumed as relish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To preserve food (or sometimes other things) in a salt, sugar or vinegar solution.","To remove high-temperature scale and oxidation from metal with heated (often sulphuric) industrial acid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glowing pickle demonstration","blocks":[{"text":"Applying electric current across a pickle causes it to glow. A moist pickle contains salt as a result of the pickling process, which allows it to conduct electricity. Ions of sodium and other substances within the pickle emit light as a result of atomic electron transitions.‍ The pickle only glows at the bottom end because it is where the brine collects. The glowing pickle is used to demonstrate ionic conduction and atomic emission in chemistry classes,‍ and also as a demonstration in lighting classes.‍"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png/330px-Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glowing_pickle_demonstration"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png/500px-Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png/1280px-Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png/500px-Glowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pickle glowing when an electric current is passed through it","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlowing-pickle-elfi-von-fliegenpilz.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Na-D-sodium_D-lines-589nm.jpg/500px-Na-D-sodium_D-lines-589nm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Na-D-sodium_D-lines-589nm.jpg/500px-Na-D-sodium_D-lines-589nm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emission spectrum of sodium.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANa-D-sodium_D-lines-589nm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Transformer-220.jpg/500px-Transformer-220.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Transformer-220.jpg/1280px-Transformer-220.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Transformer-220.jpg/500px-Transformer-220.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A variable transformer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATransformer-220.jpg"}],"sounds":{"electric":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"htt